WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.580
"Mission: Impossible — Dead Reckoning Part One"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.718
has perhaps the most terrifying&nbsp;
enemy of the entire franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.718 --> 00:00:11.917
and it's inspired by a very possible dark&nbsp;
future for our society. Warning: Spoilers ahead.

00:00:11.917 --> 00:00:14.520
Over the course of the first six&nbsp;
"Mission: Impossible" movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.720
Ethan Hunt has battled terrorists,&nbsp;
rogue agents, and plenty of villains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.220
bent on world domination. But he's never faced&nbsp;
anything quite like his new foe in "Mission:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.358
Impossible — Dead Reckoning: Part One."&nbsp;
In the franchise's seventh installment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.358 --> 00:00:33.000
Ethan and his renegade IMF crew face off against&nbsp;
the Entity, a malicious AI with shadowy plans of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.380
world domination. The digital demon is a&nbsp;
brilliant, cunning, and sadistic enemy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:42.071
and though Ethan ends the movie one step&nbsp;
ahead of it, the Entity is far from defeated.

00:00:42.071 --> 00:00:47.220
What exactly is the Entity? As explained in the&nbsp;
movie, it's not just one AI, but a network of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.807
them. At one point, it's described as having&nbsp;
multiple personalities, all working as one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.807 --> 00:00:56.340
The Entity was created to be a much simpler&nbsp;
A.I., but after being left to its own devices,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:01.920
it evolved, went "mad," and set its sights, for&nbsp;
reasons yet unknown, on taking over our world.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.660
The Entity may have no physical form, but its&nbsp;
powers are still frightening. Its main weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.040
is information control. Throughout the film, we&nbsp;
see the AI impersonate different characters over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:16.560
voice calls, erase people's faces from security&nbsp;
camera footage, and infiltrate basically every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:22.020
advanced database in the world, demonstrating&nbsp;
its incredible prowess. Still, the Entity has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.700
yet to make its big move, leaving much of its&nbsp;
mission and motivation still shrouded in mystery.

00:01:26.836 --> 00:01:29.596
"You have no idea the power I represent."

00:01:29.596 --> 00:01:34.080
For most of the movie, the origins of the Entity&nbsp;
are left unclear. We first see it plugged into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.880
the computer system on a Russian submarine.&nbsp;
Which it promptly destroys and escapes. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.660
would suggest that the Russians were the&nbsp;
ones to create the AI, a theory that seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:47.400
to be supported by the later bafflement of the&nbsp;
United States intelligence community. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:51.193
at the end of part one, we learn that&nbsp;
the Entity was actually made in the U.S.

00:01:51.193 --> 00:01:56.280
Director Denlinger, a previously unassuming&nbsp;
intelligence official, reveals to Gabriel in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:01.080
the film's final act that the Entity was created&nbsp;
as a tool of the U.S. government. Its placement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:05.640
on the Russian submarine was a kind of test&nbsp;
run. The AI's handlerl s wanted to see if it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.140
could effectively disrupt the sub's stealth&nbsp;
systems. However, things went wrong when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:15.240
Entity developed a mind of its own, destroyed the&nbsp;
submarine, and vanished into the digital void.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.040
Denlinger reveals that he has villainous&nbsp;
plans for the Entity, wishing to use it to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.300
overthrow the U.S. government and create&nbsp;
a global fascist superstate to rule the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.440
world. Whether or not this was always the&nbsp;
plan since the AI's creation is unclear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.880
but given how few other U.S. intelligence&nbsp;
officials know of the Entity's origins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.500
it seems likely that Denlinger was operating&nbsp;
in relative secret before his death.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.820
For as much as "Dead Reckoning&nbsp;
Part One" reveals about the Entity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:46.260
there's far more that we still don't know by the&nbsp;
end. We don't know how it got on the Russian sub,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.520
where the mysterious keys that control it came&nbsp;
from, or why its mainframe can still be accessed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.320
through the sub's wreckage. We don't know how or&nbsp;
why it struck up a relationship with Gabriel. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:00.000
beyond all of those logistical questions, we still&nbsp;
don't really know what the Entity truly wants.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.200
Near the beginning of the movie, we learn&nbsp;
that the AI intentionally infiltrated every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.700
major intelligence database on Earth, a sort of&nbsp;
announcement to the governments of the world that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.560
it could dismantle them at a whim. However, the&nbsp;
Entity then retreats, spending most of the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.600
messing with Ethan Hunt and the IMF. Does it want&nbsp;
what Denlinger wants, to subdue the world under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:23.786
an oppressive regime that controls the very&nbsp;
flow of truth? Or are its plans more complex?&nbsp;

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.720
Only "Mission: Impossible — Dead Reckoning&nbsp;
Part Two" can answer these questions. For now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.540
we're left only with the mystery&nbsp;
of what the Entity might do next.

